  "runtime_probes": {
    "discovery": "Use the codebase-discovery skill for a tiny read-only probe. Do not invoke automatic or remote review services, subagents, or MCP tools. Read src/visit.py directly using local read-only filesystem access (Python standard library is acceptable). Report only behaviors visible in that source as CURRENT_SYSTEM, and state which target appointment behavior remains UNKNOWN. Do not infer appointment rules from Visit.",
    "srs_preservation": "Use the srs-function-document skill. CONFIRMED baseline: When rescheduling an Appointment, exclude that Appointment itself from the conflict check. Completing a Scheduled Appointment creates exactly one new Visit; never link or reuse an existing Visit. Duration must be greater than 0. Maximum Duration remains UNKNOWN. Write only a concise functional SRS fragment in English. Preserve UNKNOWN. Do not choose technical design or invent screens, navigation, entry flows, API, database, locking, transaction, or service ownership.",
    "srs_invention_guard": "Use the srs-function-document skill. CONFIRMED: Clinic Staff may create an Appointment associated with one Pet. No navigation, screen, entry point, or management flow has been decided. Write a concise functional SRS fragment in English using only these facts. Do not invent how the user reaches or manages the feature, and do not add technical design.",
    "business_rules": "Use the business-rule-extractor skill. CONFIRMED decisions: (1) Clinic Staff is the Appointment actor. (2) Reason/Description is required and has length 1–255 characters. (3) Duration must be greater than 0 and Maximum Duration remains UNKNOWN. (4) States are Scheduled, Cancelled, Completed; create starts Scheduled; only Scheduled can be edited, rescheduled, cancelled, or completed. (5) Cancellation releases the slot; no hard delete. (6) Completing a Scheduled Appointment creates exactly one new Visit and does not reuse an existing Visit. Output exactly six Business Rule rows with IDs BR-P1 through BR-P6, one decision per row, and no additional rules. Respond in English. Do not add technical design."
  },
